Header rows are removed from the data. A column's name joins the
non-empty header texts above it with \code{" / "}, merging repeats that a
\code{colspan} created. Blank names become \code{V1}, \code{V2}, ... by column
position, and duplicates are made unique with \code{\link[=make.unique]{make.unique()}}. Names are
not otherwise made syntactic.

Cell text follows \code{\link[=html_text_clean]{html_text_clean()}}. All columns are character unless
\code{convert = TRUE}.
